\n100: - [x] T013 [P] Lane E. Run the brief-cost hook children with `TMPDIR` inside the sandbox, test first (`MBC`, `MBCT`, `RAR`). In `MBCT`, let the hook stub append `process.env.TMPDIR` to the file that `COST_PROBE_FILE` names, only when that variable is set, so the two existing cases are unchanged. Add `runs each hook child with TMPDIR inside its sandbox`: run the script with `COST_PROBE_FILE` inside the test root, and expect every recorded path to have a base name starting `ssa-cost-`, to differ from the test's own `tmpdir()` and to be gone after the run. Run `V tests/measure-brief-cost.vitest.ts` and see 1 failed, the new case. Then in `MBC`, add `TMPDIR: socketDir` to the child environment at line 167, with a comment saying the hook writes its health records under the OS temp folder, so a cost run points that folder at its own sandbox and leaves the operator's health log alone. In `RAR`, in the `measure-brief-cost.mjs` paragraph, add ``Each hook child runs with `TMPDIR` set to the sandbox, so a cost run writes no health record into the shared metrics folder.`` Verify: `node --check $MBC` exits 0, `V tests/measure-brief-cost.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and 3 passed, and `rg -c 'TMPDIR: socketDir' $MBC` prints 1.\n101: \n102: ### Wave 2\n103: - [x] T014 Lane A. Regenerate the bridges under the new name and move the typed-attach cases (`$ADV/lib/command-attach.ts`, `$ADV/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` and the `DER` outputs). After T006 and T008, rewrite the comment above the longest-key rule in `command-attach.ts`, outside the marked blocks, so its example of one command name inside another is generic, `/group:name` inside `/group:name-parent`, because no real pair is left. Run `DER`. In the guards test, change the four `/create:skill` inputs and expectations to `/create:sk-skill`. Verify: `DRV` prints `\"changed\": []` and exits 0, `OLD $ADV/lib $ADV/scripts/command-bridges $ADV/scripts/skill_advisor.py $ADV/tests` prints nothing, `rg -c 'command-create